              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सवेरो (savero) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from savela, \"in time, early\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants. CDIAL gives no Marwari form in this entry (CDIAL 13291); the match is through Hindi sawerā and Gujarati saverā. It is built on sa-, \"with\", and velā, \"time\"."
